{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656284",
      "title": "Navigating with Router Links",
      "lectureOrder": 452,
      "videoOrder": 414,
      "sourceHash": "c7c172a0c935455951b70a19807f4b4ec32a357f7c1d6e122161f5e72ff3f606",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 5.4,
          "en": "-: In the last lecture, we made our routing work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 7.89,
          "en": "We added routes and we gave Angular a place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.89,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "to load our currently active component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "But one issue we have is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "right now we can only navigate around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "by manually typing it here in the address bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 18.99,
          "en": "Not super convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.99,
          "end": 21.24,
          "en": "And while it is important to be able to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.24,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "load a route directly from the address bar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 26.94,
          "en": "it would also be nice to have some working links here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.94,
          "end": 30.15,
          "en": "in our navigation to have these tabs work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.15,
          "end": 33.27,
          "en": "So let's add some links to our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.27,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "And if we go to our app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 37.5,
          "en": "we see, here's our navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.5,
          "end": 39.337,
          "en": "The first thing you might think about is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.337,
          "end": 41.523,
          "en": "\"Hey, we can or we already have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.523,
          "end": 44.19,
          "en": "this href attribute here to be precise.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.19,
          "end": 46.11,
          "en": "So here we could have href,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 48.66,
          "en": "we'll just slash load our root route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 48.66,
          "end": 51.15,
          "en": "Here we could have /servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.15,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "And here we could have /users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "And if we now save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "we added all the routes, the paths we set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 62.13,
          "en": "in our routes configuration to our navigation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.13,
          "end": 64.71,
          "en": "And hence if this reloads and we click the tabs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.71,
          "end": 66.45,
          "en": "Hey, does this indeed working?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66.45,
          "end": 67.98,
          "en": "Now we are correctly loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 67.98,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "the route you want to load.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "Okay, this tab is not updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 73.26,
          "en": "but I will come back to this later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 73.26,
          "end": 75.21000000000001,
          "en": "But the reloading is working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 75.21000000000001,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "And that's the issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 77.94,
          "en": "It's reloading the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 77.94,
          "end": 80.34,
          "en": "Watch this reload icon here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 80.34,
          "end": 81.42,
          "en": "Do you see this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 81.42,
          "end": 85.14,
          "en": "We refresh the app with every link we click.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 85.14,
          "end": 86.94,
          "en": "And that's the natural behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 86.94,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "because with every link we click,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 90.96000000000001,
          "en": "a new request gets sent to the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 90.96000000000001,
          "end": 92.64,
          "en": "and it returns as a new page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 92.64,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "And since this page is still our Angular app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 97.22999999999999,
          "en": "with the routes registered on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 97.22999999999999,
          "end": 99.50999999999999,
          "en": "it is able to give us the correct route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 99.50999999999999,
          "end": 100.92,
          "en": "So, the same thing happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 100.92,
          "end": 103.62,
          "en": "as if we entered this manually here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 103.62,
          "end": 106.05,
          "en": "That, however, is not the best behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 106.05,
          "end": 108.42,
          "en": "because it means it restarts our app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 108.42,
          "end": 110.03999999999999,
          "en": "on every navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 110.03999999999999,
          "end": 110.87299999999999,
          "en": "That of course means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 110.87299999999999,
          "end": 113.1,
          "en": "our whole application state will be lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 113.1,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "and it might not really be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 117.15,
          "en": "the behavior we want to offer to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 117.15,
          "end": 120.48,
          "en": "So this is not how you should implement navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 120.48,
          "end": 122.313,
          "en": "How should you implement it then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 126.57,
          "en": "There is a special directive Angular gives us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 126.57,
          "end": 129.9,
          "en": "Let's get rid of all these href attributes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 129.9,
          "end": 132.9,
          "en": "So this is not how we will navigate around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 132.9,
          "end": 136.35,
          "en": "Instead, let's use this special directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 136.35,
          "end": 138.84,
          "en": "It's called \"routerLink.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 138.84,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "Now, routerLink like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 143.94,
          "en": "simply is able to parse a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 143.94,
          "end": 145.8,
          "en": "where we could pass just slash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 145.8,
          "end": 149.55,
          "en": "So just this string, slash to routerLink here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 149.55,
          "end": 152.94,
          "en": "Now this will tell Angular that this element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 152.94,
          "end": 154.5,
          "en": "on which routerLink is placed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 154.5,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "this anchor tag here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 158.55,
          "en": "will serve as a link in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 158.55,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "but it will handle a click differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "as you will see in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "Let's now also add this to the Servers link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "So routerLink equals /servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 170.19,
          "en": "And I will come back to how you may write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 170.19,
          "end": 172.92000000000002,
          "en": "the path here in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 172.92000000000002,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "And our way of using routerLink is with property binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 180.33,
          "en": "so you can enclose it in square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 180.33,
          "end": 183.45,
          "en": "And now of course you can't just pass /users here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 183.45,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "because this would now search",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "for a property with that name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 189.45,
          "en": "which would even be an invalid name in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 189.45,
          "end": 191.64,
          "en": "So now you have to pass a string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 191.64,
          "end": 193.387,
          "en": "with single quotation marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 193.387,
          "end": 195.54,
          "en": "-: -or, better--an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 195.54,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "which gives you a more fine-grain control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 198.61,
          "en": "over routerLink.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 198.61,
          "end": 200.76,
          "en": "And I will come back to this later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 200.76,
          "end": 202.59,
          "en": "when this is especially useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 202.59,
          "end": 205.56,
          "en": "Here, in this array, you now specify",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 205.56,
          "end": 207.96,
          "en": "all these segments of your path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 207.96,
          "end": 209.91,
          "en": "as elements in this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 209.91,
          "end": 211.14,
          "en": "So, the first segment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 211.14,
          "end": 215.73,
          "en": "in this case is only a string: /users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 215.73,
          "end": 218.73,
          "en": "and if you had /users, /something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 218.73,
          "end": 220.44,
          "en": "you would have a second element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 220.44,
          "end": 223.89,
          "en": "which is then just something without a slash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 223.89,
          "end": 225.51,
          "en": "The leading slash here is only needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 225.51,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "to make this an absolute path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 229.47,
          "en": "and I will come back to this in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 229.47,
          "end": 231.12,
          "en": "For now, we'll get rid of this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 231.12,
          "end": 233.97,
          "en": "Now, this array notation is not super convenient,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 233.97,
          "end": 235.98,
          "en": "but soon you will see when it really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 235.98,
          "end": 238.71,
          "en": "gives you an advantage or when you need this notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 238.71,
          "end": 242.97,
          "en": "It allows you to construct more complex paths very easily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 242.97,
          "end": 245.79,
          "en": "So with this, we set up our three links using routerLink,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 245.79,
          "end": 248.61,
          "en": "either by passing a string or this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 248.61,
          "end": 252.27,
          "en": "which allows us to define our individual path elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 252.27,
          "end": 254.73,
          "en": "With that, if we save this and have a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 256.89,
          "en": "at our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 256.89,
          "end": 259.68,
          "en": "now you see it's still reloads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 259.68,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "or it still gives us the components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 262.95,
          "en": "but it doesn't reload the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 262.95,
          "end": 266.52,
          "en": "If you watch this reload icon, nothing is happening there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 266.52,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "Because routerLink catches the click on the element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 271.53,
          "en": "prevents the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 271.53,
          "end": 273.6,
          "en": "which would be to send a request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 273.6,
          "end": 276.54,
          "en": "and instead analyzes what we passed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 276.54,
          "end": 278.13,
          "en": "to the routerLink directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 278.13,
          "end": 281.58,
          "en": "So, this path or this array of path elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 281.58,
          "end": 284.7,
          "en": "And then parses it and checks if it finds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 284.7,
          "end": 287.28,
          "en": "a fitting route in our configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 287.28,
          "end": 288.63,
          "en": "which it of course does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 288.63,
          "end": 291.54,
          "en": "because we defined all the paths we're using here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 291.54,
          "end": 293.88,
          "en": "And this is how we can navigate around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 293.88,
          "end": 295.26,
          "en": "with the routerLink.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 295.26,
          "end": 298.23,
          "en": "And this actually is how we should navigate around,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 298.23,
          "end": 300.69,
          "en": "because it gives us the better user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 300.69,
          "end": 302.37,
          "en": "It doesn't restart our app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 302.37,
          "end": 304.38,
          "en": "therefore it keeps the app state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 304.38,
          "end": 308.07,
          "en": "and it's much faster than reloading the page all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 308.07,
          "end": 311.1,
          "en": "You can of course still type something here manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 311.1,
          "end": 312.51,
          "en": "so that will still work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 312.51,
          "end": 315.12,
          "en": "But if you're inside of the app using routerLink,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 315.12,
          "end": 316.203,
          "en": "it's much better.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
